{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And they did so, as He commanded, etc.</b> The reason He doubled the phrase ״כֵן כַּאֲשֶׁר״ etc. — and one of them alone would not have sufficed — is that it intends two things: the first, that they did the things thus; and the second, that they did not do them until Pharaoh asked them for the sign, as HaShem had commanded." "<b>Further,</b> it intends that since the sign would proclaim the strengthening of their prophecy in order that they be believed, Scripture testifies concerning them that they did not do the thing for the sake of this consideration, but rather to perform the commandment of HaShem. And this is its saying <b>as HaShem commanded</b>, for performing the commandment of HaShem is more precious to the righteous than any desire in the world."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:31.610703559Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}